.TH DBG2ELF 1 "November 2026" "um80 0.4.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dbg2elf \- write an ELF file with DWARF from prog.dbg, for GDB with a Z80 target
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dbg2elf
[\fB\-o\fR \fIprog.elf\fR]
[\fB\-\-comp\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR]
[\fB\-\-asm\-lines\fR \fBauto\fR|\fBalways\fR|\fBnever\fR]
[\fB\-\-keep\-underscore\fR]
[\fB\-\-keep\-case\fR]
[\fB\-\-no\-variables\fR]
[\fB\-\-ix\-locals\fR \fBfbreg\fR|\fBoff\fR]
[\fB\-\-language\fR \fBc\fR|\fBasm\fR]
.I prog.dbg
[\fIprog.com\fR]
.br
.B dbg2elf \-\-unwinder\-path
.br
.B dbg2elf \-\-vars\-path
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dbg2elf
reads
.IR prog.dbg ,
the file that
.B "ul80 \-\-debug\-info"
writes, and the program file.
dbg2elf writes
.IR prog.elf ,
an ELF32 file with the code, the routine symbols, DWARF line rows,
inlined calls, and the variables and types.
GDB with a Z80 target reads
.I prog.elf
and debugs the program on
.BR "cpmemu \-\-gdb" .
.PP
The program file is the file that
.I prog.dbg
names, or
.IR prog.com .
dbg2elf checks the length and the SHA-256 of the program file.
A
.I prog.dbg
from an older build gives an error, and dbg2elf writes no ELF file.
.PP
The file has
.B e_machine
220 (EM_Z80), so GDB sets the z80 architecture from the file.
The line table is DWARF 4.
.PP
GDB also needs two Python scripts from the um80 package.
.B udb80_unwind.py
unwinds the Z80 stack for
.BR bt ,
.BR up ,
.B finish
and
.BR next .
.B udb80_vars.py
adds the commands
.BR zlocals ,
.BR zargs ,
.B zprint
and
.B zptype
for the variables that DWARF cannot describe, for example a variable in a
register.
The options
.B \-\-unwinder\-path
and
.B \-\-vars\-path
print where the scripts are.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o " \fIFILE\fR, " \-\-output " \fIFILE\fR"
The ELF file.
The default is
.I prog.elf
beside
.IR prog.dbg .
.TP
.BI \-\-comp\-dir " DIR"
The directory that relative source paths start from.
The default is the directory of
.IR prog.dbg .
The compilers write paths relative to the directory where you ran them.
.TP
.BR \-\-asm\-lines " auto|always|never"
Write the lines of the
.I .mac
files.
.B auto
(the default) writes the lines only when
.I prog.dbg
has no source lines, so an assembler program has lines.
.B always
also writes the lines of the
.I .mac
files for the bytes that have no source line.
A step then goes into the runtime.
.B never
writes none.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-underscore
Keep the leading underscore of a C name.
Without the option, GDB sees
.B main
for
.BR _main .
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-case
Keep the case of a label.
um80 writes each label in upper case.
Without the option, dbg2elf writes a label that has no lower case letter
in lower case.
A name from a
.B ;#func
marker keeps its case.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-variables
Write no variables and no types.
.TP
.BR \-\-ix\-locals " fbreg|off"
The variables at IX+N.
.B fbreg
(the default) writes them with
.BR DW_OP_fbreg .
The values are correct only when GDB has loaded
.BR udb80_unwind.py .
.B off
writes no record for them.
.B udb80_vars.py
still reads them.
.TP
.BR \-\-language " c|asm"
The language of the compile unit.
The default is
.BR c .
.TP
.B \-\-unwinder\-path
Print the path of
.B udb80_unwind.py
and stop.
.TP
.B \-\-vars\-path
Print the path of
.B udb80_vars.py
and stop.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the usage and stop.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
dbg2elf wrote the ELF file, or printed a path.
.TP
.B 1
dbg2elf could not read
.IR prog.dbg ,
or the program file does not agree with
.IR prog.dbg .
.TP
.B 2
An option is not correct.
.SH EXAMPLES
Build a C program, write the ELF file, and debug the program with GDB:
.PP
.nf
.RS
LIB=$(uc80 \-\-print\-lib\-dir)
uc80 \-g \-o prog.mac prog.c
um80 \-\-debug\-info \-o prog.rel prog.mac
ul80 \-\-debug\-info \-o prog.com prog.rel $LIB/libc.lib $LIB/runtime.lib
dbg2elf prog.dbg
.RE
.fi
.PP
In one terminal:
.PP
.nf
.RS
cpmemu \-\-gdb prog.com
.RE
.fi
.PP
In a second terminal:
.PP
.nf
.RS
gdb \-ex "source $(dbg2elf \-\-unwinder\-path)" \e
    \-ex "source $(dbg2elf \-\-vars\-path)" prog.elf
(gdb) target remote :1234
(gdb) break prog.c:4
(gdb) continue
(gdb) bt
.RE
.fi
.PP
GDB prints a warning about
.B _break_handler
when GDB connects.
Ignore the warning.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
dbg2elf and the two scripts are in um80 0.4.0 and later
.RB ( "pip install \(dqum80>=0.4.0\(dq" ).
GDB must have the Z80 target (GDB 11.1 and later).
A GDB built with
.B \-\-enable\-targets=all
has the target.
The Homebrew formula
.B gdb
uses that option.
.B "cpmemu \-\-gdb"
is in cpmemu 4.11.0 and later.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I prog.dbg
The linked debug file from
.BR "ul80 \-\-debug\-info" .
.TP
.I prog.elf
The output file.
.TP
.I um80/gdb/udb80_unwind.py
The GDB unwinder.
.TP
.I um80/gdb/udb80_vars.py
The GDB variable commands.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR udb80 (1),
.BR ul80 (1),
.BR um80 (1),
.BR gdb (1)
.PP
docs/gdb.md and docs/debug_info.md of um80_and_friends:
https://github.com/avwohl/um80_and_friends
